    <string name="about_write_to" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Write to %1$s</string>
    <string name="about_no_mail_app" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">No email app is installed. The address is %1$s.</string>
    <string name="privacy_who_title" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Who we are</string>
    <string name="privacy_who" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">This app is made by wander wildwood, an independent developer: one person, not a company. That makes wander wildwood the data controller for anything the app itself handles, and that is very little: what you put in stays on this phone unless you send it somewhere yourself, and nothing comes to the developer.</string>
    <string name="privacy_contact_title" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">How to contact us</string>
    <string name="privacy_contact" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Write to email@wanderthe.dev, about your data or anything else.</string>
    <string name="privacy_rights_title" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Your rights</string>
    <string name="privacy_rights" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Under the GDPR you can ask to see the data held about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to limit or object to its use, to take a copy with you, to withdraw consent, and to complain to a data protection authority. Since the app keeps what it stores only on your phone, you can do most of this yourself: clear your statistics in the app, clear the app\'s data in Android\'s settings, or uninstall the app.</string>
